+XIV. Erratum E6 — Coverage-Disclosed Dynasty Scoring (OWNER-RATIFIED)
+Ratified 2026-11-16 (#235 6937184242; formal ruling 6937295727, Option 1: no official rankings across
+different coverage profiles). Text as drafted (Kimi’s final draft incorporating GPT’s refinements, #235
+6937172806). Supersedes, in full, the “missing-axis weight renormalize+journal” clause of Annex B
+dynasty-score-v1. This erratum controls wherever the two conflict.
+1. Abeyance, not redistribution. A missing axis holds its ratified weight in abeyance. Its weight is
+never redistributed among present axes, by any mechanism, without explicit owner ratification under
+AA10.
+2. Three reported quantities. Every score emission reports, as distinct fields: coverage (sum of
+present-axis weights); observed weighted average (weighted mean across present axes only, using
+original relative weights); weighted subtotal (observed weighted average × coverage). No partial score
+may be displayed, stored, or transmitted without all three fields and the list of missing axes.
+3. No cross-coverage comparison. Lineages with different coverage profiles are never ranked against
+each other. Any comparison requires identical formula version and identical coverage profile. Displaying
+coverage beside a leaderboard does not make incomparable measurements comparable.
+4. Journal-derived only. Inputs are verified journal events exclusively. Proposals, predictions, self-
+reported achievements, and observer interpretations are not evidence and can never become scored
+facts.
+5. No retroactive completeness. When a missing axis becomes measurable, prior score records are
+unchanged; each record permanently carries the coverage profile at its tick. Historical comparison uses
+like-for-like records only.
+6. Determinism. Same journal + same formula version + same tick →same three quantities, bit-for-bit.
+Replay must reproduce any displayed score (AT-18).
+7. Read-only oracle. Scores are projections. They never enter the action-validation path, never modify
+the journal, never confer legitimacy. The observer interprets evidence; it cannot manufacture it.
+Formula-ID handling (GPT’s formulation, accepted by Kimi): the formula ID/version is declared in an
+authoritative configuration or genesis record (the AA8 precedent — the engine journals the formula ID
+at genesis); the observer reads that declaration and the journal and deterministically recomputes. The
+observer itself never writes.
+Territory (owner ruling 6937295727 item 2): the territorial-control definition remains RESERVED. The
+territory-years axis is reported MISSING until the owner separately ratifies a definition; no lane
+defines or implements one in the meantime.
